From 4ab25c8b2e3959854d6c2ddf745b0088fdf13373 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noel Blatter <noel.blatter@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:37:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Start-up: multihost_utils stays unloaded through the first
 device_put

jax._src.dispatch imports jax.experimental.multihost_utils inside the function behind
the first device_put (the first jnp.asarray of a run) and uses it for sharded arrays
only. The module is in LAZY_MODULES, but the finder that hands out the lazy loader is
removed when import jax has finished, so the module was executed in full, together with
jax._src.prng, jax.sharding and jaxlib.gpu_prng. It is now created lazily right before
the finder goes (LAZY_LATE_MODULES). Anything that uses it later gets the real module.

First jnp.asarray in Docker (arm64 Linux, one CPU): 1.8 to 2.1 ms -> 0.24 to 0.34 ms.
Build phase of the grid benchmark, twelve fresh runs in turn: 9.8 -> 8.3 ms on arm64
Linux, 64.5 -> 61.9 ms in the emulated x86-64 image.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../__pycache__/_startup.cpython-312.pyc      | Bin 43492 -> 44006 bytes
 differometor/_startup.py                      |  14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

